    "discipline": "Civil",
    "subject": "Construction Engineering",
    "chapter": "Project Administration",
    "topic": "Management",
    "subtopic": "Overview",
    "content_html": "<div class= \"container-fluid\">\r\n  <div class= \"row align-items-start\">\r\n    <div class=\"col col-lg-8\">\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>Construction management is the planning, coordination, and control of a construction project from inception to completion.</li>\r\n<li>It involves managing resources, time, cost, quality, and safety to ensure project success.\r\n<li>Responsibilities of project managers include project planning, scheduling, budgeting, and quality control.</li>\r\n<li>Pre-construction involves planning, design, and procurement. The construction phase is where physical work occurs, and post-construction includes closeout and occupancy.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n    </div>\r\n    <div class=\"col\">\r\n<center><p><img src=\"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/b/bb/Project_Management_%28phases%29.png\" style=\"max-width: 50vh;\"></p><br/>\r\n<small><small><a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Project_Management_(phases).png\">Alphamu57</a>, <a href=\"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\">CC BY-SA 4.0</a>, via Wikimedia Commons</small></small></center><br/>\r\n    </div>\r\n  </div>\r\n</div>",
