    "discipline": "Civil",
    "subject": "Fluid Mechanics",
    "chapter": "Scaling Laws for Fans, Pumps and Compressors",
    "topic": "Efficiency of a Centrifugal Pump",
    "subtopic": "Overview",
    "content_html": "<h2 id=\"mechanical-efficiency\">Mechanical efficiency:</h2>\r\n\r\n<p>The power at the shaft of the centrifugal pump is more than the power available at the impeller of the pump. The ratio of the power available at the impeller to the power at the shaft of the centrifugal pump is known as mechanical efficiency.</p>\r\n\r\n<p><span class=\"math display\">\\[\\large \\eta =\\frac{\\mathrm{Power\\ at\\ the\\ impeller}}{\\mathrm{Power\\ at\\ the\\ shaft}}\\]</span></p>",
    "important": "",
