    "discipline": "Civil",
    "subject": "Mathematics and Statistics",
    "chapter": "Calculus",
    "topic": "Application of Derivatives",
    "subtopic": "Curvature of Any Curve",
    "content_html": "<h5><span><b>Curvature of Any Curve:</b></span></h5>\r\n<div class=\"container-fluid\">\r\n\t<div class=\"row align-items-start\">\r\n\t\t<div class=\"col col-lg-8\">\r\n\r\n<div class=\"text-center\">\r\n  <button type=\"button\" class=\"btn btn-light shadow-lg\">$K = \\dfrac{y''}{(1 + (y')^2)^{3/2}}$ <span class=\"text-muted\">&emsp; &emsp; &emsp; Page 46</span></button>\r\n</div><br/>\r\n\r\n<p>If the equation of the curve is easier to differentiate with respect to x, then:</p>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"text-center\">\r\n  <button type=\"button\" class=\"btn btn-light shadow-lg\">$K = \\dfrac{- x''}{(1 + (x')^2)^{3/2}}$ <span class=\"text-muted\">&emsp; &emsp; &emsp; Page 46</span></button>\r\n</div><br/>\r\n\r\n<h5><span><b>Radius of Curvature:</b></span></h5>\r\n\r\n\r\n<p>The radius of curvature R at any point on a curve is defined as the absolute value of the reciprocal of the curvature K at that point.</p>\r\n<div class=\"text-center\">\r\n  <button type=\"button\" class=\"btn btn-light shadow-lg\">$R = \\dfrac{1}{\\mid K \\mid}.... K \\neq0$ <span class=\"text-muted\">&emsp; &emsp; &emsp; Page 46</span></button>\r\n</div><br/>\r\n\r\n\t\t</div>\r\n    \t\t<div class=\"col\">\r\n     <center><img src=\"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/3/31/Radius_of_curvature.gif\" alt=\"Radius of curvature\" width=\"340\"><br/>\r\n<small><small><a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Radius_of_curvature.gif\">Kiatdd</a>, <a href=\"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0\">CC BY-SA 3.0</a>, via Wikimedia Commons</small></small></center><br/>\r\n    \t\t</div>\r\n  \t</div>\r\n</div>",
    "important": "Curvature of a curve:\r\n\\[K = \\dfrac{y''}{\\left(1 + (y')^2\\right)^{3/2}}\\]\r\n\r\nRadius of Curvature:\r\n\\[R = \\dfrac{1}{|K|}\\]",
    "resources": "<div class=\"mt-4 pt-4 border-t border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-700 flex flex-wrap gap-2\"><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1XJ0DQ8xO1Vg5-pUsO-ryQU0MFzSUHB_f/preview\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"px-3 py-1.5 bg-blue-100 dark:bg-blue-900/40 text-blue-700 dark:text-blue-300 rounded text-xs font-bold hover:bg-blue-200 transition-colors\">📄 Homework</a><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/17xo9l1pcn40WpVx8dJfp0XR-JldgI775/preview\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"px-3 py-1.5 bg-green-100 dark:bg-green-900/40 text-green-700 dark:text-green-300 rounded text-xs font-bold hover:bg-green-200 transition-colors\">✅ Solution</a><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1YY-g1tjxrS8PH4IsOZaXR8FUzxom5gWe/preview\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"px-3 py-1.5 bg-purple-100 dark:bg-purple-900/40 text-purple-700 dark:text-purple-300 rounded text-xs font-bold hover:bg-purple-200 transition-colors\">👨‍🏫 Tutoring</a><!-- <div class=\"w-full mt-2\"><div style=\"padding:56.25% 0 0 0;position:relative;\"><iframe src=\"https://player.vimeo.com/video/829775199?h=884354ed22&amp;badge=0&amp;autopause=0&amp;player_id=0&amp;app_id=58479\" frameborder=\"0\" allow=\"autoplay; fullscreen; picture-in-picture\" allowfullscreen style=\"position:absolute;top:0;left:0;width:100%;height:100%;\" title=\"Application of Derivatives- Radius of Curvature\"></iframe></div><script src=\"https://player.vimeo.com/api/player.js\"></script>\r\n\r\n<div style=\"padding:56.25% 0 0 0;position:relative;\"><iframe src=\"https://player.vimeo.com/video/829774872?h=120a4dfa50&amp;badge=0&amp;autopause=0&amp;player_id=0&amp;app_id=58479\" frameborder=\"0\" allow=\"autoplay; fullscreen; picture-in-picture\" allowfullscreen style=\"position:absolute;top:0;left:0;width:100%;height:100%;\" title=\"Application of Derivatives- Maxima and Minima\"></iframe></div><script src=\"https://player.vimeo.com/api/player.js\"></script></div> --></div>",
    "images": [],
    "local_images": [],
    "video": "assets/videos/Radius_of_Curvature_Formula_in_Terms_of_First_and_Second_Derivatives.mp4",
    "videoTitle": "Radius of Curvature Formula in Terms of First and Second Derivatives"
