    "subject": "Mathematics and Statistics",
    "chapter": "Measures of Central Tendencies",
    "topic": "Standard Deviation and Variance",
    "subtopic": "Overview",
    "content_html": "<div class=\"container-fluid\">\r\n\t<div class=\"row align-items-start\">\r\n\t\t<div class=\"col col-lg-6\">\r\n\r\n<p>The variance of the population is the arithmetic mean of the squared deviations from the population mean. If <span class=\"math inline\">\\(\\mu\\)</span> is the arithmetic mean of a discrete population of size N, the <strong>population variance</strong> is defined by: \r\n\\[\\sigma^2 = \\dfrac{1}{N} \\left[(X_1 - \\mu)^2 + (X_2 - \\mu)^2 + .... + (X_N - \\mu)^2 \\right]\\]\r\n<div class=\"text-center\">\r\n  <button type=\"button\" class=\"btn btn-light shadow-lg\">$\\sigma^2= \\dfrac{1}{N} \\displaystyle \\sum_{i=1}^N (X_i - \\mu)^2$ <span class=\"text-muted\">&emsp; &emsp; &emsp; Page 63</span></button>\r\n</div><br/>\r\n\r\n<p>If your data set is a sample from a population, the variance of that sample is calculated by dividing the sum of the squared deviations by the number of data points minus one (N-1). So, <strong>sample variance</strong> is: \r\n\r\n\\[s^2= \\dfrac{1}{n-1} \\left[(X_1 - \\bar{X})^2 + (X_2 - \\bar{X})^2 + .... + (X_N - \\bar{X})^2 \\right]\\]\r\n<div class=\"text-center\">\r\n  <button type=\"button\" class=\"btn btn-light shadow-lg\">$s^2= \\dfrac{1}{n-1} \\displaystyle \\sum_{i=1}^n (X_i - \\bar{X})^2$ <span class=\"text-muted\">&emsp; &emsp; &emsp; Page 63</span></button>\r\n</div><br/>\r\n<b>Population</b> standard deviation is given by:\r\n<div class=\"text-center\">\r\n  <button type=\"button\" class=\"btn btn-light shadow-lg\">$\\sigma= \\sqrt{\\dfrac{1}{N} \\displaystyle \\sum_{i=1}^N (X_i - \\mu)^2}$ <span class=\"text-muted\">&emsp; &emsp; &emsp; Page 63</span></button>\r\n</div><br/>\r\n\r\n<b>Sample</b> standard deviation is given by:\r\n<div class=\"text-center\">\r\n  <button type=\"button\" class=\"btn btn-light shadow-lg\">$s= \\sqrt{\\dfrac{1}{n-1} \\displaystyle \\sum_{i=1}^n (X_i - \\bar{X})^2}$ <span class=\"text-muted\">&emsp; &emsp; &emsp; Page 63</span></button>\r\n</div><br/>\r\n\r\n\r\n\t\t</div>\r\n    \t\t<div class=\"col\">\r\n     <center><img src=\"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/c/c6/Visualization_of_standard_deviation.svg\" alt=\"Sample Standard Deviation\" style=\"max-width: 50vh;\"><br/>\r\n<small><small><a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Visualization_of_standard_deviation.svg\">Thebiologyprimer</a>, <a href=\"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\">CC BY-SA 4.0</a>, via Wikimedia Commons</small></small></center><br/>\r\n    \t\t</div>\r\n  \t</div>\r\n</div>",
    "important": "Population variance,\r\n\\[\\begin{align*} \r\n\\sigma^2 &amp;= \\dfrac{1}{N} \\left[(X_1 - \\mu)^2 + (X_2 - \\mu)^2 + .... + (X_N - \\mu)^2 \\right]\\\\ &amp;= \\dfrac{1}{N} \\Sigma (X_i - \\mu)^2\r\n\\end{align*}\\]\r\n\r\nSample variance,\r\n\\[\\begin{aligned} \\sigma^2 &amp;= \\dfrac{1}{N-1} \\left[(X_1 - \\mu)^2 + (X_2 - \\mu)^2 + .... + (X_N - \\mu)^2 \\right]\\\\ &amp;= \\dfrac{1}{N-1} \\Sigma (X_i - \\mu)^2\\end{aligned}\\]",
    "resources": "<div class=\"mt-4 pt-4 border-t border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-700 flex flex-wrap gap-2\"><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1XglFw0BBWnzQo0bQ1jiYEBqxrEtwVpaE/preview\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"px-3 py-1.5 bg-blue-100 dark:bg-blue-900/40 text-blue-700 dark:text-blue-300 rounded text-xs font-bold hover:bg-blue-200 transition-colors\">📄 Homework</a><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1mctycJb2BWNoAVI2xLqLxQ1KuUC0zWpv/preview\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"px-3 py-1.5 bg-green-100 dark:bg-green-900/40 text-green-700 dark:text-green-300 rounded text-xs font-bold hover:bg-green-200 transition-colors\">✅ Solution</a><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1NKbt9UcpUZH-8g7T_4dD1ptGV_N3eemV/preview\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"px-3 py-1.5 bg-purple-100 dark:bg-purple-900/40 text-purple-700 dark:text-purple-300 rounded text-xs font-bold hover:bg-purple-200 transition-colors\">👨‍🏫 Tutoring</a></div>",
