    "topic": "Column Buckling",
    "subtopic": "Concentrically loaded long Columns",
    "content_html": "<h5><span><b>Concentrically loaded long Columns:</b></span></h5>\r\n\r\n<p>Euler’s Formula:</p>\r\n<div class=\"text-center\">\r\n<button type=\"button\" class=\"btn btn-light shadow-lg\">$P_{cr} = \\dfrac{\\pi ^{2}EI}{(Kl)^{2}}$ <span class=\"text-muted\">&emsp; &emsp; &emsp; Page 137</span></button>\r\n</div><br/>\r\nwhere,<br />\r\n$P_{cr}$ = critical axial loading<br />\r\nl = unbraced column length<br />\r\nK = effective length factor to account for end supports<br />\r\n$\\dfrac{l}{r}$ = slenderness ratio for the column</p>",
    "important": "Critical axial loading:\r\n\\[P_{cr} = \\dfrac{\\pi ^{2}EI}{(Kl)^{2}}\\]\r\n\r\nSlenderness ratio: \\(\\dfrac{l}{r}\\)",
