    "discipline": "Civil",
    "subject": "Mechanics of Materials",
    "chapter": "Columns",
    "topic": "Column Buckling",
    "subtopic": "Equivalent Length",
    "content_html": "<h5><span><b>Equivalent Length:</b></span></h5>\r\n\r\n<center><img src=\"https://onedrive.live.com/embed?resid=9C913AE725AFDEB1%21636&authkey=%21ALSWdaldO4J5nUg&width=934&height=409\" width=\"934\" height=\"409\" /></center>\r\n\r\n<p>When column has both ends hinged, its entire length gets buckled to form a bow. Therefore equivalent length of a column with both ends hinged is ‘L’. It is written as L$_e$<br />\r\nFor other end conditions, equivalent lengths forming a bow are:</p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n\t<li>Both ends hinged $L_e$= L,</li>\r\n\t<li>One end fixed and other free L$_e$= 2L</li>\r\n\t<li>One end fixed other hinged L$_e$= $\\dfrac{L}{\\sqrt{2}}$</li>\r\n\t<li>Both ends fixed L$_e$= $\\dfrac{L}{2}$</li>\r\n</ul>",
