    "content_html": "<p>When the equations of static equilibrium are insufficient to solve number of unknowns in the system, the beam is said to be statically indeterminate beam. In such case, we have to use some additional equations, such as from deflection formula, etc to completely solve the beam and get all unknown support reactions and moments.</p>",
