    "discipline": "Civil",
    "subject": "Structural Engineering",
    "chapter": "Design of Steel Components",
    "topic": "Tension Members",
    "subtopic": "Overview",
    "content_html": "<div class= \"container-fluid\">\r\n  <div class= \"row align-items-start\">\r\n    <div class=\"col col-lg-8\">\r\n   <p>Tension members are structural components designed to primarily carry axial loads in tension, which means they are subjected to forces pulling them apart. They are commonly used in various structural applications, including truss members, cables, rods, and suspension elements.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Tension members are designed to meet structural safety and serviceability requirements.\r\nDesign factors include selecting an appropriate cross-sectional shape, determining the minimum required section area, and providing adequate connection details.</p>\r\n    </div>\r\n    <div class=\"col\">\r\n<center><p><img src=\"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/d/d7/PAIRED_END_POSTS_AT_MID_SPAN_SHOWING_CONNECTION_OF_DIAGONAL_TENSION_MEMBERS_WITH_ANCHOR_CASTING._-_Baltimore_and_Ohio_Railroad%2C_Bollman_Truss_Bridge%2C_Spanning_Little_Patuxent_River_HAER_MD%2C14-SAV%2C1-17.tif\" style=\"max-width: 50vh;\"></p><br/>\r\n<small><small><a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:PAIRED_END_POSTS_AT_MID_SPAN_SHOWING_CONNECTION_OF_DIAGONAL_TENSION_MEMBERS_WITH_ANCHOR_CASTING._-_Baltimore_and_Ohio_Railroad,_Bollman_Truss_Bridge,_Spanning_Little_Patuxent_River_HAER_MD,14-SAV,1-17.tif\">Lowe, Jet, creator</a>, Public domain, via Wikimedia Commons</small></small></center><br/>\r\n    </div>\r\n  </div>\r\n</div>",
