    "chapter": "Basic Hydraulics",
    "topic": "Open-Channel Flow",
    "subtopic": "Overview",
    "content_html": "<p>Open channel flow refers to the flow of water in natural or artificial channels, where the flow is free to interact with the atmosphere. Open channel flow principles are applied to a wide range of engineering projects, including the design of irrigation canals, river channel modifications, and stormwater management systems.</p>",
